          "n": 1,
          "text": "to add force to them, and may be rendered by ‘indeed.’ Comp",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "Prasannarâghava p. 77 or Bhâminîvilâsa I., 98 or Vairâgyas'ataka",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "St. 60. It is not, I think, the disjunctive वा here. It may be",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "noted that the word इव is also somewhat similarly used as in क इव",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "बहुमानः in Vairâgyas'ataka St. 25 or in Kirâta I., 31 and it is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "further worthy of note that वा is विकल्पे or उपमायाम्. See the quo-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "tation in Mallinâtha’s commentary on Mâgha XVIII., 1 and",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "Siddh. Kaum. I., 55. In English too, the following expressions",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "may be compared. ‘No such thing.’ ‘By what manner of means",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "did he &c.” On the other hand, may not the word have some",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "connexion with the वा or वाव of the Upanishads ? वाव stands before",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "consonants and वा generally before vowels; this might perhaps",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "lead one to suppose that वा is there a substitute by Sandhi for वै",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 14,
          "text": "(see for instance S'ârîraka Bhâshya p. 54 and gloss on it). But a",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 15,
          "text": "passage in the Kaushîtaki Upanishad militates against this view.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 16,
          "text": "See p. 19. (Bibl. Ind. Ed.). See also the passage from the S'ata-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 17,
          "text": "paṭha Brâhmaṇa quoted at 2 Muir’s Texts 353 (New Ed.). Since",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 18,
          "text": "writing the above, I have found that Dr. Kielhorn has explained",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 19,
          "text": "the word differently and as a disjunctive. See Panchatantra I., p.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 20,
          "text": "7. notes (Bomb. Classics).—Anushṭub.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XXXIII.—After मूर्ध्नि सर्वस्य लोकस्य a word like तिष्ठेत् or वर्तेत",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "should be supplied and then the construction becomes easy.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "For द्वयीवृत्तिः the reading of some of the copies compare Vîra-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "charita 81 (Trithen’s Ed.). The idea of placing flowers and",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "garlands on heads is very common in Sanskṛit Literature. In-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "stances need scarcely be quoted. We, however, could scarce-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "ly speak of such a thing in our days except in speaking of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "ladies.—Anushṭub.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XXXIV.—वैरायते. Denominative = वैरं करोति see Pâṇini III.,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
